From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 108/108] v4l2object: Don't remove fields from caps the caller
 can't change

set_format_full() removes colorimetry or interlace-mode from the caps when
the driver returns values GStreamer doesn't know. A decoder passes its
shared input caps, giving "gst_structure_remove_field: assertion
'IS_MUTABLE (structure)' failed" on every MJPEG stream into v4l2jpegdec
on cedrus. Only change writable caps.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
index 493f19d..3f3ec9c 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
@@ -4433,7 +4433,8 @@ gst_v4l2_object_set_format_full (GstV4l2Object * v4l2object, GstCaps * caps,
     /* The driver (or libv4l2) is miss-behaving, just ignore interlace-mode from
      * the TRY_FMT */
     disable_interlacing = TRUE;
-    if (gst_structure_has_field (s, "interlace-mode"))
+    if (gst_caps_is_writable (caps) &&
+        gst_structure_has_field (s, "interlace-mode"))
       gst_structure_remove_field (s, "interlace-mode");
   }
 
@@ -4447,7 +4448,8 @@ gst_v4l2_object_set_format_full (GstV4l2Object * v4l2object, GstCaps * caps,
     /* The driver (or libv4l2) is miss-behaving, just ignore colorimetry from
      * the TRY_FMT */
     disable_colorimetry = TRUE;
-    if (gst_structure_has_field (s, "colorimetry"))
+    if (gst_caps_is_writable (caps) &&
+        gst_structure_has_field (s, "colorimetry"))
       gst_structure_remove_field (s, "colorimetry");
   }
 
